      ":question/worked-solution": "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202u}{\u2202y}=\\frac{\u2202u}{\u2202r}\\sin \\theta+\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{\u2202u}{\u2202\\theta}\\cos \\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $u$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202u}{\u2202r}=- 8 r,\\,\\frac{\u2202u}{\u2202\\theta}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202u}{\u2202y} & =(- 8 r)\\sin \\theta+\\frac{1}{r}(0)\\cos \\theta \\\\ & =- 8 r \\sin {\\theta}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
